  "summary": "The near-future as imagined with cassette-era tech: chunky CRTs, tape drives, amber phosphor and beige industrial futures.",
  "description": "Cassette futurism (French formicapunk) describes futures built from 1977-1993 hardware: Alien's Nostromo terminals, WarGames mainframes, Blade Runner's video phones, (Alien, 1979) beige server rooms and tape reels. Unlike raypunk's finned rockets, its future is dust-covered, ad-hoc and analog-plausible. CARI documented it (2017+); it rules modern \"analog sci-fi\" art and games (Alien: Isolation, Signalis).",
